WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.667 --> 00:00:03.467
♪♪

00:00:03.467 --> 00:00:07.100
-I want to start by saying,
if you can sense a vibe...

00:00:07.100 --> 00:00:09.033
Are you [bleep] kidding me?

00:00:09.033 --> 00:00:10.701
[ Laughter ]

00:00:10.701 --> 00:00:13.701
Wally and Scollins
come in chatting it up.

00:00:17.067 --> 00:00:19.067
During "Corrections."

00:00:21.133 --> 00:00:25.634
Is nothing sacred
in this place?

00:00:25.634 --> 00:00:27.534
Was that one of
the guild requests?

00:00:27.534 --> 00:00:30.734
"I wanna be able to talk
during 'Corrections.'"

00:00:30.734 --> 00:00:32.667
[ Laughter ]

00:00:41.634 --> 00:00:43.300
Well.

00:00:45.868 --> 00:00:49.367
I apologize
that you had to see that.

00:00:49.367 --> 00:00:51.701
But if you don't shame them
in the moment,

00:00:51.701 --> 00:00:53.534
they don't learn their lesson.

00:00:58.534 --> 00:01:01.601
I was gonna open
by explaining...

00:01:01.601 --> 00:01:03.567
[ Laughter ]

00:01:05.801 --> 00:01:08.167
..."Corrections" is gonna be
a little looser.

00:01:08.167 --> 00:01:10.167
[ Laughter ]

00:01:10.167 --> 00:01:13.334
And I realize I betrayed that
right off the bat.

00:01:13.334 --> 00:01:14.667
But one of the reasons

00:01:14.667 --> 00:01:19.501
"Corrections" is gonna have
a different vibe now

00:01:19.501 --> 00:01:23.834
is that it is no longer
Emmy-nominated.

00:01:23.834 --> 00:01:25.701
For two years,
it was Emmy-nominated.

00:01:25.701 --> 00:01:29.968
And then during the strike,
it was un-nominated,

00:01:29.968 --> 00:01:32.133
I think is the term they use.

00:01:32.133 --> 00:01:35.334
If you don't get nominated, you
just don't find out anything.

00:01:35.334 --> 00:01:37.334
If you were nominated
and then you're not,

00:01:37.334 --> 00:01:40.000
they call you

00:01:40.000 --> 00:01:42.067
and they request
that you stop

00:01:42.067 --> 00:01:45.501
describing the work
as Emmy-nominated.

00:01:45.501 --> 00:01:48.534
But, you know,
the thing about that is

00:01:48.534 --> 00:01:50.367
I...

00:01:50.367 --> 00:01:52.133
I feel as though
a burden has been lifted,

00:01:52.133 --> 00:01:54.467
because I will admit
that it went to my head

00:01:54.467 --> 00:01:56.267
and I did start chasing
the Emmy gold.

00:01:56.267 --> 00:01:58.334
I didn't start
doing the corrections

00:01:58.334 --> 00:02:00.534
I thought were important to do.
I started doing the corrections

00:02:00.534 --> 00:02:03.701
that I thought the voters
would want me to do.

00:02:03.701 --> 00:02:05.767
[ Laughter ]

00:02:05.767 --> 00:02:09.968
And now I can just go back
to the integrity of the work,

00:02:09.968 --> 00:02:13.434
which is what
this has always been.

00:02:13.434 --> 00:02:14.801
Because I think,
when done right,

00:02:14.801 --> 00:02:18.634
this is unlike anything
you watch on...

00:02:18.634 --> 00:02:20.634
I don't know, your phone?

00:02:20.634 --> 00:02:22.634
[ Laughter ]

00:02:22.634 --> 00:02:25.968
Propped against the toaster
while you're drinking coffee.

00:02:29.167 --> 00:02:32.234
So, with that relief that
this is no longer a show

00:02:32.234 --> 00:02:34.934
that is Emmy-nominated,
came enthusiasm as I jumped

00:02:34.934 --> 00:02:38.901
into the comments
of our viewers today.

00:02:38.901 --> 00:02:43.868
And the first comment
I read said,

00:02:43.868 --> 00:02:46.100
"I was surprised
he hasn't been doing these.

00:02:46.100 --> 00:02:48.801
I thought he could do
'Corrections' during the strike

00:02:48.801 --> 00:02:50.467
because the only thing
the writers provide

00:02:50.467 --> 00:02:52.801
is forced laughter."

00:02:52.801 --> 00:02:55.667
[ Laughter ]

00:02:55.667 --> 00:02:58.267
I don't need writers

00:02:58.267 --> 00:02:59.934
to provide forced laughter.

00:02:59.934 --> 00:03:01.667
I got Buck.

00:03:01.667 --> 00:03:03.734
[ Laughter ]

00:03:05.167 --> 00:03:07.834
And that's not forced laughter.

00:03:07.834 --> 00:03:09.501
Now, don't get me wrong.

00:03:09.501 --> 00:03:12.834
I'm sure when he was a kid,
somebody forced him to laugh...

00:03:15.367 --> 00:03:16.701
...and now he can't stop.

00:03:16.701 --> 00:03:18.200
I mean, I think
we're dealing with

00:03:18.200 --> 00:03:20.767
some sort of deep-seated trauma

00:03:20.767 --> 00:03:23.601
that every one of these works.

00:03:23.601 --> 00:03:27.133
"Bucky, come over to your mama.
I'm funny, aren't I, Bucky?"

00:03:27.133 --> 00:03:28.467
[ Laughter ]

00:03:28.467 --> 00:03:30.434
"Oh, Bucky, I don't know
what I'd do

00:03:30.434 --> 00:03:33.734
if my baby didn't think
I was funny.

00:03:33.734 --> 00:03:35.567
Bucky."

00:03:35.567 --> 00:03:37.767
[ Laughter ]

00:03:41.367 --> 00:03:42.801
Is it worth...

00:03:42.801 --> 00:03:44.434
Here's a question we had.

00:03:44.434 --> 00:03:45.601
When we did our first show
on Monday,

00:03:45.601 --> 00:03:47.033
was it worth doing
"A Closer Look"

00:03:47.033 --> 00:03:48.334
that covered
the last five months?

00:03:48.334 --> 00:03:51.601
Is it worth...
Same question.

00:03:51.601 --> 00:03:53.834
Is it worth doing
a "Corrections"

00:03:53.834 --> 00:03:56.467
and going back and correcting
the last week of shows

00:03:56.467 --> 00:03:59.801
we did five months ago
that went uncorrected.

00:03:59.801 --> 00:04:01.601
Because people won't even
remember the errors

00:04:01.601 --> 00:04:02.934
from five months ago.

00:04:02.934 --> 00:04:04.267
It is worth it,
because I remember.

00:04:04.267 --> 00:04:06.567
I have a photographic memory
of this show.

00:04:06.567 --> 00:04:10.501
I have basically
spent five months

00:04:10.501 --> 00:04:13.334
eating myself up inside
due to the mistakes

00:04:13.334 --> 00:04:14.767
I made
that I had not addressed.

00:04:14.767 --> 00:04:17.634
So I am going to start
by addressing mistakes

00:04:17.634 --> 00:04:19.901
from five years ago
that I still remember.

00:04:19.901 --> 00:04:22.100
Five months ago.
Excuse me.

00:04:22.100 --> 00:04:24.267
Here's the first one.

00:04:24.267 --> 00:04:27.667
The call with Aunt Joan
said "slide to answer."

00:04:27.667 --> 00:04:29.601
That means the call
hadn't been answered yet.

00:04:29.601 --> 00:04:31.033
It was still
an incoming call.

00:04:31.033 --> 00:04:32.634
The [bleep]?

00:04:32.634 --> 00:04:34.567
[ Laughter ]

00:04:36.968 --> 00:04:38.801
The sun doesn't go
behind the moon.

00:04:38.801 --> 00:04:41.901
The moon goes
in front of the sun.

00:04:41.901 --> 00:04:44.701
The easiest way to remember
that is I don't sit

00:04:44.701 --> 00:04:47.033
behind a standing Shoemaker
at a meeting.

00:04:47.033 --> 00:04:50.367
I sit, and then he comes
and stands in front of me.

00:04:50.367 --> 00:04:52.601
[ Laughter ]

00:04:52.601 --> 00:04:54.901
Apologies, by the way,
to Shoemaker's neighbors.

00:04:54.901 --> 00:04:57.234
Can't imagine you had
a good five months.

00:04:57.234 --> 00:04:59.267
[ Laughter ]

00:05:04.501 --> 00:05:07.000
Our last episode,
we made a lot of fun

00:05:07.000 --> 00:05:11.100
about Tucker Carlson
getting fired from Fox News.

00:05:11.100 --> 00:05:13.767
Joke's on us.
Guy landed on his feet.

00:05:15.767 --> 00:05:19.133
Oh, another guy we made fun of
our last show, Ron DeSantis.

00:05:19.133 --> 00:05:20.634
We did an impression of him

00:05:20.634 --> 00:05:23.300
eating pudding
with three fingers.

00:05:23.300 --> 00:05:24.634
And a jackal asked,

00:05:24.634 --> 00:05:27.801
"Why are you so sure
the three figures --

00:05:27.801 --> 00:05:30.834
the three fingers
are contiguous?"

00:05:30.834 --> 00:05:32.434
And I think,
knowing Ron DeSantis

00:05:32.434 --> 00:05:34.601
and how weird he is,

00:05:34.601 --> 00:05:37.133
I'm pretty confident
it might be like...

00:05:39.701 --> 00:05:41.367
...this.

00:05:41.367 --> 00:05:43.734
[ Laughter ]

00:05:47.701 --> 00:05:50.300
I don't think he's gonna
be president, guys.

00:05:50.300 --> 00:05:51.801
[ Laughter ]

00:05:51.801 --> 00:05:53.133
Before the break,
we were talking about

00:05:53.133 --> 00:05:55.901
the Stevie Nicks song
"White Winged Dove."

00:05:55.901 --> 00:05:58.167
A lot of you told me the name
of the song is "Edge of 17."

00:05:58.167 --> 00:06:01.200
And not to give a correction
to a legend like Stevie Nicks,

00:06:01.200 --> 00:06:03.334
but just [bleep] change it.

00:06:03.334 --> 00:06:05.534
Don't "Baba O'Riley"
your songs.

00:06:05.534 --> 00:06:08.434
Make it be the title
people want it to be.

00:06:08.434 --> 00:06:10.534
You know, when you do that,
that just means some [bleep]

00:06:10.534 --> 00:06:12.467
at a karaoke night
gets to run the computer

00:06:12.467 --> 00:06:13.634
and people go up
and they're like,

00:06:13.634 --> 00:06:15.200
"I would love to do
'White Winged Dove.'"

00:06:15.200 --> 00:06:18.701
He's like, "I can't find it.

00:06:18.701 --> 00:06:20.567
I don't think it's a song."

00:06:22.701 --> 00:06:25.467
Someone said the sound
Stevie Nicks makes in that song

00:06:25.467 --> 00:06:26.968
sounds more like an owl
than a dove.

00:06:26.968 --> 00:06:28.167
And I thought,
Oh, I know what I'll do.

00:06:28.167 --> 00:06:30.033
I'll say,
"Oh, let's take a listen,"

00:06:30.033 --> 00:06:33.000
and I'd play a clip
from that song.

00:06:33.000 --> 00:06:34.534
And then we'd put in,
you know,

00:06:34.534 --> 00:06:37.300
an actual owl's hoots
over the doves.

00:06:37.300 --> 00:06:39.167
But I can't do that.
The reason we didn't do that

00:06:39.167 --> 00:06:43.667
is when you use a song,
due to music licensing,

00:06:43.667 --> 00:06:45.000
it can't be on YouTube.

00:06:45.000 --> 00:06:46.334
And I'm not complaining.

00:06:46.334 --> 00:06:48.234
That's the rule
for everything.

00:06:48.234 --> 00:06:50.067
You know, we put a song
in "Corrections,"

00:06:50.067 --> 00:06:51.567
it comes off YouTube.

00:06:51.567 --> 00:06:53.734
Same is true
of "Carpool Karaoke."

00:06:54.734 --> 00:06:56.834
[ Laughter ]

00:07:03.234 --> 00:07:04.567
By the way,
I don't want to...

00:07:04.567 --> 00:07:07.567
I already regret being critical
of Stevie Nicks.

00:07:07.567 --> 00:07:10.467
That is not someone
you want to run afoul of.

00:07:10.467 --> 00:07:14.567
You ever listen to the lyrics
of "Silver Springs"?

00:07:14.567 --> 00:07:16.734
Ask Lindsey Buckingham.

00:07:16.734 --> 00:07:18.300
Because if you run afoul
of Stevie Nicks,

00:07:18.300 --> 00:07:20.300
you wake up in the morning...

00:07:20.300 --> 00:07:22.667
just a scarf on your pillow.

00:07:26.501 --> 00:07:29.934
Oh, people say, "What's in your
drink, and do you finish it?"

00:07:29.934 --> 00:07:33.267
It is a negroni,
and I do finish it.

00:07:33.267 --> 00:07:34.834
Not during "Corrections."

00:07:34.834 --> 00:07:37.767
I stay here the whole weekend,

00:07:37.767 --> 00:07:39.000
in the dark,

00:07:39.000 --> 00:07:40.767
just slowly sipping it,
and I try to finish

00:07:40.767 --> 00:07:43.467
right before
Monday's "Closer Look."

00:07:45.634 --> 00:07:49.400
We said Donald Trump
has been indicted three times,

00:07:49.400 --> 00:07:52.000
which was one more
than the Unabomber.

00:07:52.000 --> 00:07:54.267
And then I said,
"Who, as the Una implies,

00:07:54.267 --> 00:07:55.467
just had the one."

00:07:55.467 --> 00:07:57.901
I put that in.
Really liked it.

00:07:57.901 --> 00:08:01.133
Nary a laugh from the audience.

00:08:01.133 --> 00:08:03.667
And then a bunch of you
said the Una in Unabomber

00:08:03.667 --> 00:08:05.033
was for his bombing targets.

00:08:05.033 --> 00:08:07.968
The U-N was for universities,
the A was for airlines.

00:08:07.968 --> 00:08:12.100
A Uni-bomber would be someone
who bombs only once.

00:08:12.100 --> 00:08:14.934
Like me when I told
the Unabomber joke.

00:08:14.934 --> 00:08:17.100
[ Laughter ]

00:08:17.100 --> 00:08:21.234
And thanks to our eagle-eyed
viewer who sent in all that

00:08:21.234 --> 00:08:23.734
Unabomber information,
Conner O'Malley.

00:08:23.734 --> 00:08:25.734
[ Laughter ]

00:08:29.567 --> 00:08:31.868
We said Trump looked like
a Klingon general in court

00:08:31.868 --> 00:08:33.567
and then showed a picture
of Worf

00:08:33.567 --> 00:08:36.167
from "Star Trek:
The Next Generation."

00:08:36.167 --> 00:08:39.467
He was a lieutenant,
I was told by a bunch of people.

00:08:39.467 --> 00:08:42.701
That was a bad choice
for a Klingon general.

00:08:42.701 --> 00:08:44.767
General Martok
would have worked.

00:08:47.033 --> 00:08:50.868
I don't like the expression
"you people,"

00:08:50.868 --> 00:08:53.367
because it usually implies
the speaker has

00:08:53.367 --> 00:08:56.834
some pretty bad prejudices.

00:08:56.834 --> 00:08:58.334
With that said,
I'd just like to say

00:08:58.334 --> 00:08:59.734
to the Star Trek fans
out there --

00:08:59.734 --> 00:09:01.300
you people.

00:09:01.300 --> 00:09:02.901
[ Laughter ]

00:09:04.434 --> 00:09:05.834
We also said you could
never be a general

00:09:05.834 --> 00:09:08.834
because the Starfleet uses
the ranks of the Navy.

00:09:08.834 --> 00:09:12.000
Because I guess in the future,
space is water.

00:09:14.400 --> 00:09:16.501
Taco Bell has had breakfast
since 2014.

00:09:16.501 --> 00:09:18.834
They just added
the breakfast taco.

00:09:18.834 --> 00:09:20.634
What's going on over there?

00:09:20.634 --> 00:09:23.033
[ Laughter ]

00:09:23.033 --> 00:09:25.367
Got to be stoned
to work there, too?

00:09:30.234 --> 00:09:33.868
Aaron Rodgers did not,
as I said yesterday,

00:09:33.868 --> 00:09:36.567
tear his ACL.

00:09:36.567 --> 00:09:39.734
He tore his Achilles.

00:09:39.734 --> 00:09:42.234
That's the last time
I do my own research.

00:09:42.234 --> 00:09:44.367
[ Laughter ]

00:09:47.601 --> 00:09:49.934
I said Laphonza Butler
is the first

00:09:49.934 --> 00:09:51.534
Black lesbian woman
in the Senate.

00:09:51.534 --> 00:09:54.200
I was told lesbian
and woman are redundant.

00:09:54.200 --> 00:09:55.901
And then I decided to say
that information

00:09:55.901 --> 00:09:58.133
as flatly as possible
and move on.

00:10:05.367 --> 00:10:09.968
I don't love giving corrections
to my colleagues,

00:10:09.968 --> 00:10:13.267
but oftentimes they don't have
a way to give them.

00:10:13.267 --> 00:10:16.467
We showed a clip
of Sean Hannity,

00:10:16.467 --> 00:10:19.033
and it's about how Trump

00:10:19.033 --> 00:10:20.434
was gonna be
the next House speaker.

00:10:20.434 --> 00:10:25.167
And instead of former,
they said "fromer."

00:10:25.167 --> 00:10:26.501
Which I think
is maybe how they...

00:10:26.501 --> 00:10:28.801
Like, if Trump calls up angrily
and he's like,

00:10:28.801 --> 00:10:31.801
"I'm not the former president,"
they're like, "Fromer."

00:10:38.067 --> 00:10:41.067
A lot of people said that's not
where their ears would be.

00:10:41.067 --> 00:10:43.267
[ Laughter ]

00:10:51.167 --> 00:10:52.501
Ah.

00:10:54.901 --> 00:10:58.133
We showed Trump Tower.

00:10:58.133 --> 00:11:00.534
We made it look like
"The Honeymooners."

00:11:00.534 --> 00:11:02.200
And someone said,

00:11:02.200 --> 00:11:03.634
"Oh, my God, you should do
'Honeymooners.'"

00:11:03.634 --> 00:11:05.901
This is like not a correction.
This is like a pitch.

00:11:05.901 --> 00:11:07.033
Like, "You should do a bit

00:11:07.033 --> 00:11:08.968
where Trump's like,
'To the moon, Mel.'"

00:11:08.968 --> 00:11:10.367
But, like, you have
to remember, like,

00:11:10.367 --> 00:11:13.701
Trump would not have any power
in that relationship.

00:11:13.701 --> 00:11:15.534
If Trump was like Ralph Kramden,
he'd be like,

00:11:15.534 --> 00:11:16.701
"To the moon, Mel."

00:11:16.701 --> 00:11:18.033
She'd be like,
"I'll tell them everything,"

00:11:18.033 --> 00:11:20.534
And he'd be like,
"Look who's back from the moon."

00:11:23.434 --> 00:11:25.434
I forgot we had a P.O. Box,

00:11:25.434 --> 00:11:29.234
so it was fun to come in
and see some stuff.

00:11:29.234 --> 00:11:32.501
I've got...
I got top three.

00:11:32.501 --> 00:11:35.634
Someone said, you know,

00:11:35.634 --> 00:11:38.300
"Sorry you didn't get nominated
for an Emmy."

00:11:38.300 --> 00:11:40.968
But again, don't be sorry.
It's a relief.

00:11:40.968 --> 00:11:42.968
[ Laughter ]

00:11:42.968 --> 00:11:47.634
Imagine how mad I'd be
if this was Emmy-nominated

00:11:47.634 --> 00:11:50.634
and [bleep] Scollins and Wally
are just walking in...

00:11:50.634 --> 00:11:53.300
[ Laughter ]

00:11:53.300 --> 00:11:54.934
You guys remember,
this all started with Legos.

00:11:54.934 --> 00:11:57.267
Somebody made a Lego me,
and they...

00:11:57.267 --> 00:11:59.601
That's a little Emmy.

00:11:59.601 --> 00:12:01.834
I would've put it in the hand,
but it doesn't fit in the hand,

00:12:01.834 --> 00:12:03.834
which I feel like
might be the joke.

00:12:03.834 --> 00:12:05.534
[ Laughter ]

00:12:11.267 --> 00:12:16.200
And that is a Mac Tonight
with a jackal in his pocket.

00:12:16.200 --> 00:12:18.534
And I don't know
if you can see this.

00:12:18.534 --> 00:12:21.200
I couldn't quite understand
what they're doing here.

00:12:21.200 --> 00:12:23.767
It says -- There's a picture
of a Pizza Hatz

00:12:23.767 --> 00:12:25.601
that I guess goes on it,
but it's hard to read.

00:12:25.601 --> 00:12:28.400
But it says,

00:12:28.400 --> 00:12:32.267
"Accessories sold separately."

00:12:32.267 --> 00:12:33.767
So they made me a present

00:12:33.767 --> 00:12:36.434
and showed me a picture
of another thing they made,

00:12:36.434 --> 00:12:38.434
and I guess I gotta buy it.

00:12:38.434 --> 00:12:40.167
[ Laughter ]

00:12:42.300 --> 00:12:45.701
But then someone took the cake.

00:12:45.701 --> 00:12:48.200
I mean, they said...
Somebody made this and said,

00:12:48.200 --> 00:12:50.267
"I'm willing
to give you the patent" --

00:12:50.267 --> 00:12:53.434
I mean, they wanted
to split the money.

00:12:53.434 --> 00:12:55.667
Sell it at the NBC Store.

00:12:55.667 --> 00:12:59.901
And it's for the Seth fans
who are also jackal fans.

00:13:02.234 --> 00:13:04.701
[ Laughter ]

00:13:09.734 --> 00:13:12.567
[ Laughter continues ]

00:13:12.567 --> 00:13:15.400
I mean, it's the most
haunting thing I've ever seen.

00:13:18.133 --> 00:13:19.734
And you know, now...

00:13:23.868 --> 00:13:26.834
Now is when I weigh something,
right?

00:13:26.834 --> 00:13:30.133
Like, I laid in

00:13:30.133 --> 00:13:31.801
that if Stevie Nicks
is mad at you,

00:13:31.801 --> 00:13:34.234
she leaves a scarf
on your pillow,

00:13:34.234 --> 00:13:36.234
and I feel like
it didn't get anything.

00:13:39.601 --> 00:13:41.501
And so, like, I've set
something up and I'm like,

00:13:41.501 --> 00:13:43.200
now do I call it back
by revealing

00:13:43.200 --> 00:13:46.234
that I've run a scarf
up my sleeve?

00:13:46.234 --> 00:13:48.200
[ Laughter ]

00:13:50.801 --> 00:13:52.467
Like, does that pay off at all?

00:13:55.834 --> 00:13:58.334
[ Chuckles ]

00:13:58.334 --> 00:14:00.434
I think we're a little rusty.

00:14:00.434 --> 00:14:02.868
[ Laughter ]

00:14:02.868 --> 00:14:05.534
Some people forgot
what time it started.

00:14:05.534 --> 00:14:07.167
[ Laughter ]

00:14:09.200 --> 00:14:11.000
But you know what?

00:14:11.000 --> 00:14:14.000
[Bleep]
I hate to say it.

00:14:14.000 --> 00:14:17.734
Missed you guys.
Missed the jackals.

00:14:17.734 --> 00:14:19.601
Codependency.
I've made a codependency

00:14:19.601 --> 00:14:21.434
with a bunch of [bleep] jackals.

00:14:25.667 --> 00:14:27.501
It's great to be back.
And...

00:14:27.501 --> 00:14:29.300
[ Laughter ]

00:14:42.400 --> 00:14:44.801
You know, as I'm --
as I'm watching this

00:14:44.801 --> 00:14:46.467
in the monitor...

00:14:49.234 --> 00:14:50.367
...one thing really...

00:14:50.367 --> 00:14:51.701
There's like one thought
I'm having.

00:14:51.701 --> 00:14:53.868
This shouldn't be
Emmy-nominated.

00:14:53.868 --> 00:14:55.801
[ Laughter ]

00:14:55.801 --> 00:14:57.133
See me next week.

